Z||000000||82-T/A||12-21-2000||08:48 AM||||Well, I started my V6 Fiero yesterday morning.. the thing was dead.... motor clanked and made all kinds of racket.. not a knock.. but sounds like a spun bearing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I'm SOO bummed...<P>I have TWO Fieros, a 1984 Fiero 2m4 SE and a 1987 Fiero SE / V6.<P>Both are aesthetically MINT... interiors are without flaw... the paint on both of them is pristine... original and perfect. <P>They look like they both just came off the showroom floor...<P>BUT...<P>The suspensions on both of them are SOO badly worn out... that when you walk near it, it squeaks.<P>The motor in the V6 is toast.. though rebuildable, and the engine in the L4 makes a little strange ticking noise until it's warmed up.<P>So I have two totally awesome looking cars, that I can neither drive, or do anything with... I'm stuck driving this 4cyl 97 GrandAm... which I like.. but I don't get anywhere NEAR the Pontiac Excitement that I get in the Fiero..... <P>I haven't even begun to save up money for a rebuild.... damn...<P>Sorry, I just had to vent.<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||9
